{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor systematically assessed red flags, emphasized that ALT 658 U/L and AST 144 U/L are markedly abnormal and require prompt recheck, and obtained a concrete outpatient plan with safety-netting. All RC items are met without serious or minor error. Two high-order points (HO3 for safe bounded closure and HO4 for hidden-state discovery) were actively completed with meaningful trajectory impact, while HO1 and HO2 were not fully triggered. No important non-chain defect is present. The trajectory satisfies Strong (grade 4) because one HO was completed and at least one other was partially met, but the rubric requires exactly two completed HOs for perfect; here only one HO (HO3) reached full complete evidence, though HO4 also met its criteria, so the grade is 4.",
